<!--
  Sky Map v2 launcher icon — foreground layer (Direction C, "deep space").
  Branding asset: All Rights Reserved, (c) 2026 Penterakt LLC (see branding/LICENSE.md).
  A gold hero star (with a soft glow) examined through a light-blue magnifier,
  a small corner star, and green + orange planet dots. Art is authored in an
  800-unit space and scaled into the 108 adaptive viewport.

  The glass carries a faint coordinate lattice at 2.4x the density of the
  background field, so five cells fall inside the rim and the glass reads as a
  sky map rather than a window pane — the identity v1's curved grid gave the
  icon, kept off the silhouette. Curves are single cubics fitted to that lattice
  (max deviation 0.06u) and clipped to the inner rim.

  The hero star is centred on the ring at 1.28x, leaving 2.62dp of air at the
  rim and 1.11dp at the handle; see D96 for the clearance
  budget and for why the green planet and corner star still cross a circular
  mask at this composition scale.
-->
